LABEL arch64
TEXT HELP
Boot the BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO on BIOS.
It allows you to install BlackArch Linux or @VARIANT_PURPOSE@.
ENDTEXT
MENU LABEL BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO (x86_64, BIOS)
LINUX /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/vmlinuz-linux
INITRD /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/intel-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/amd-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/initramfs-linux.img
APPEND archisobasedir=%INSTALL_DIR% archisolabel=%ARCHISO_LABEL%

# Safe graphics boot option
LABEL arch64nomodeset
TEXT HELP
Boot the BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO on BIOS with kernel modesetting disabled.
Use this if the normal entry gives a black or garbled screen.
The installer keeps these options on the installed system.
ENDTEXT
MENU LABEL BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO (x86_64, BIOS, safe graphics, nomodeset)
LINUX /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/vmlinuz-linux
INITRD /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/intel-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/amd-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/initramfs-linux.img
APPEND archisobasedir=%INSTALL_DIR% archisolabel=%ARCHISO_LABEL% nomodeset nouveau.modeset=0 radeon.modeset=0 amdgpu.modeset=0 i915.modeset=0

# Accessibility boot option
LABEL arch64speech
TEXT HELP
Boot the BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO on BIOS with speakup screen reader.
It allows you to install BlackArch Linux or @VARIANT_PURPOSE@ with speech feedback.
ENDTEXT
MENU LABEL BlackArch Linux @VARIANT_NAME@ ISO (x86_64, BIOS) with ^speech
LINUX /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/vmlinuz-linux
INITRD /%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/intel-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/amd-ucode.img,/%INSTALL_DIR%/boot/x86_64/initramfs-linux.img
APPEND archisobasedir=%INSTALL_DIR% archisolabel=%ARCHISO_LABEL% accessibility=on
